Replace the ad-hoc trajectory-control-plugin/DESIGN.md at the repository
root with a conforming proposed/architecture Agent Note triplet.

The note records the verified runtime position, which corrects the prior
draft in both directions: in-place rewind needs no surface-mechanism
change (anchor-to-tail replace is already expressible, with two in-tree
precedents), while two real blockers were missing — Session.append has no
ignorable writer surface, so every new event is required-on-read, and a
non-compaction user/message replacement renders as nothing because the
conversation view matches compaction by hardcoded plugin name and the
generic fallback admits only append-surface events.

Delivery moves from a dynamic Cordis plugin to in-repository packages:
new session events, new RPCs, and the conversation-view fix are all
unreachable from a dynamic package.
